WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.370
Good morning, Anne!

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.710
Diana!

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.210
Are you all right?

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.060
Yes, I am.
It just hurts a little.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.930
Don't push yourself too hard, Anne.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.390
Yes, I know.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:08.620
Let's walk carefully.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:09.880
I'm all right.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:19.590
It was October again when Anne
was ready to go back to school.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.030
Oh, it's so beautiful!

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:43.580
It's almost like the trees and the birds
are celebrating my return to school.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.150
Being alive is such a wonderful thing!

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.430
You've been in your house for too long.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.680
Good morning, Anne! It's been  a long time!

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:08.590
Good morning.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:10.320
Is your ankle all right now?

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.000
Can you walk again?

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.310
Yes, of course.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:18.850
Thank goodness. We were always
waiting for your return.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.960
Thank you, everyone!
Thank you!

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.760
Miss Stacy is playing ball!

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.420
Miss Stacy! Do your best!

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.820
Anne, Miss Stacy is really wonderful.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:51.350
Here goes!

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.450
Be careful!

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.330
Miss Stacy, hang in there!

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.780
Most of the boys lose against her.
But Gilber...

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.270
Gilbert is on par with her.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.300
Here it goes!

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:15.070
Teacher, go!

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.330
Let's stop here for this morning.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.210
All right, teacher.
We'll play again tomorrow morning!

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:41.440
Of course.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.870
Good morning, Miss Stacy.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.920
Oh, Anne Shirley!
Are you all right already?

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.600
Yes, teacher.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:57.510
Sometimes we have to deal
with difficult things.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:02.710
But it can't always be handled
with courage and feelings.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:08.820
For example, Anne shirley learned this
and had to pay with her ankle.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:15.320
But if we are to find a cause of this,

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:21.210
I think it's because your
dare game needs more rules.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.470
For example,

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:27.470
the darer must do his own dare
when the dared cannot do it.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:30.960
If there was this rule,

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:36.920
there wouldn't be any serious
danger when playing dare.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:41.030
Why do you think any kind of
sports has it's own set of rules?

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:43.230
Please think about the reason behind it.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.780
Then let's begin our lessons.

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:51.680
Today all the classes will do the same thing.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.000
What's going on?

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:53.100
What are we going to do?
What's going on?

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.100
What are we going to do?

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.930
Do you know what this flag is?

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.830
The Union Jack.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:00.830
Right.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:03.610
And this one?

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:05.880
The French flag.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.610
Every country has its own flag.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:13.970
Canada has one for each state.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:17.600
A flag can represent a country, house or state.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:24.010
But does this school of Avonlea have one?

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:25.680
No!

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.280
It hasn't!

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.130
I think we're going to make one.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.380
Let's make a school flag!

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:31.530
That's right!

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:35.830
Let's all think of a flag for
Avonlea school today.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.590
Wonderful!

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:42.310
We can use this flag to cheer in
the sports meet, for example.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:45.110
A flag can unite everyone.

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:46.310
That's right!

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:51.640
Then let's find a symbol that suits Avonlea.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:58.180
Think of something which represents Avonlea
and draw it on a sheet of paper.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.490
Yes!

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:10.820
Welcome back, Anne.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:14.210
From the way you run,
your leg should be fine.

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:15.210
Yes.

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:17.790
Oh, Marilla. Today I'm incredibly happy!

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.000
I love Miss Stacy with my whole heart.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:25.250
When she pronounces my name I feel
INSTINCTIVELY that she's spelling it with an E.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.060
Really.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.670
Of course it's not just because of that.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:32.250
She's wonderful in all aspects.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.950
What is that thing?

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:34.980
This?

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.000
It's a flag.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.160
I can see that its a flag,

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.990
but has a strange look.

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:47.090
Yes...
It didn't turn out well.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:51.940
I wanted it to represent the wood's,
but I added too many things on.

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:56.210
Miss Stacy picked up
3 pictures from the flags we did

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:58.670
that represented Avonlea the best.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.070
Of course mine didn't get chosen.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:05.690
And the best flag was chosen by everyone.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.420
The three of them were beautiful

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.760
but my favorite was the one
made by Roman Campbell.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.650
The mere glance attracts you

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:18.650
because it was very original and creative.

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:24.780
Roman was always getting scolded
by Mr. Phillips for not paying attention

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.020
and we often teased him for that.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.420
He never tried his best until now.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.510
Now I changed my opinion of him.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:39.450
And I understand that
Miss Stacy is a very fair person.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:46.690
She's not like Mr. Phillips that was always
demanding and expounding homework.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:49.180
She appears to be a good teacher.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:50.650
Doesn't she?

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:53.500
Marilla, I have no gift for art

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:57.710
but I have confidence Miss Stacy
will like my today's work.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.180
And what work is that?

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:01.910
It's a composition.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:05.070
And you know I'm good at them, don't you?

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.630
The topic is: What I want to do in my future.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:11.350
My my. It's an interesting topic.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:15.050
If it wasn't interesting enough, nobody
would be interested to write it.

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.280
After I finish my homework
I'll come to help out.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.770
You forgot to clean the milk bottle.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:39.110
Anne Shirley, you must
write a good composition.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.830
You must work hard to impress Miss Stacy.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.860
Anne, if you don't come down soon
your soup will be frozen over!

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.450
How many times do I have to call you?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.620
I'm sorry.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.600
I couldn't write a single word.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.180
Where has all that self-confidence gone?

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:08.130
You can't write the way you talk?

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:11.430
Marilla, talking and writing
are very different things.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:15.170
You have to concentrate
harder to write a good composition.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:18.950
And there's too many things to write about
this topic and it's hard to choose just one.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:22.270
I'm plain and I have a bad temper,

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:25.970
I don't think that even a
minister would like me for his wife.

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:29.750
So I'll probably will have to work for a living.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:36.180
I would like to be a teacher,

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:42.160
but I would need a higher education
and would have to study very hard.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:46.170
Now that you mentioned, your parents
were teachers, weren't they?

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:50.390
Yes. That's why I think I have the
chance to become one.

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:54.340
My mother didn't look like Miss Stacy

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:57.980
but I'm sure she was a good teacher.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:02.910
But maybe the ambition of
being a teacher is a little small.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:06.450
OH! I would love to be a trained nurse.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:12.800
Wouldn't be nice to go with the Red Crosses to
the field of battle as a messenger of mercy?

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:17.290
That is, if I don't go out
as a foreign missionary.

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:19.580
That would be very romantic!

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:25.280
But one would have to be
very good to be a missionary.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:28.190
And that would be a stumbling block.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:36.570
I think all you need to do is write about
the things you said to us just now.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:44.410
Yes, your teacher should be able to
understand what you want to say.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.890
Matthew...

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.090
Thank you, Marilla!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.920
Now it will be much easier.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.650
Well, now hurry up and eat.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:57.310
Yes. I'm very hungry now.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:14.550
Anne's hard work did not
go unnoticed by Miss Stacy.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:19.970
Anne Shirley received great honors,
and the teacher's trust.

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:25.690
But Anne was not the only one
receiving special treatment.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:31.740
Miss Stacy would take the students
out for a field trip every week,

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:35.790
teaching both theory and practicals.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:45.790
And because of the young teacher,
the Avonlea children blossomed like flowers.

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:49.170
And November came.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:55.790
Christmas is coming soon,
and I have a plan to discuss with you all.

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:58.930
As you all know Christmas is coming.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:02.820
I wish to hold a concert in
the public hall this Christmas.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:05.400
Good idea, teacher!

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:08.420
I see everyone likes the idea.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:11.920
There is a motive for this concert.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:17.730
I want to use the money to make
a flag for Avonlea School.

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:23.440
I asked everyone to draw a flag, right?

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:28.710
I want the image of that flag
to be the symbol of our school

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:32.350
and it will represent us wherever we go.

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:36.980
Diana, it's wonderful!
I always wanted to take part in a concert.

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:40.320
Teacher, what will we do in the concert?

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:45.200
We'll decide together, of course.
You will all participate in the concert.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:00.630
Then the concert will be more
than just music recitals?

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:02.090
That's right Matthew.

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.030
Because it involves the whole school,

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:07.590
Miss Stacy said each grade
will have their own performance.

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:10.910
Other than songs and
music we'll have 2 stage acts!

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.520
One will be The
Society for the Suppression of Gossip.

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:17.920
Isn't interesting?

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:18.340
Yes.

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:20.530
The other it will be
The Fairy Queen.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:23.850
I really want to take part in this one.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.570
And also in the tableau.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:27.650
A tableau?

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:30.230
That's right.
It's a scene from the Bible.

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:32.820
It's called
Faith, Hope and Charity.

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:36.200
That seems very difficult.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:42.410
Yes it is. The three of us will have to
express ourselves just by our looks.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:47.340
But with Miss Stacy's guidance
I feel I can do anything!

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:52.660
We haven't decided yet who
will play the characters, but...

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:55.490
Now I remembered,
I have to go out for a while.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.630
Oh, Diana, I really envy you.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:06.660
You'll be able to sing a solo song.

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:08.630
Anne, don't be so pessimist.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.670
You will probably take part in the drama.

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.680
I have something to confess, Diana.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:17.720
If they chose me to be the Fairy Queen,

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:21.410
I would be able to jump down into
this pool of cold water without hesitation.

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:26.010
Did I said something funny?

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:27.690
Oh, Anne...

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.010
But I don't think they will choose you.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:32.930
Oh... I never though
that my best friend Diana,

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:35.410
would make such a cruel statement!

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:37.430
Because... because...

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:38.830
Because of my hair?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:42.920
I never saw a red-haired Queen.

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:46.400
No, Diana, I won't lose hope.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:51.220
Because I don't think it would be
strange to have a red-haired Queen.

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:55.330
Otherwise red-haired girls would be pitiful.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.780
Oh... why is my hair red?

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:23.670
Then we'll decide the roles of the
6th graders for the Fairy Queen.

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:33.430
For the Fairy Queen, will be...

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:35.630
Jane Andrews.

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:41.020
You'll take the role of the Queen.
Stand up.

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:42.890
Yes, teacher.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:50.720
And the fairies will be played by
Tillie Boulter, Josie Pye and Anne Shirley.

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:54.120
What's wrong, Josie?

00:16:56.760 --> 00:17:00.010
Josie, I understand your disappointment,

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:04.060
but every role has its challenges and difficulties.

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:09.220
When you start practicing you'll
see that all roles are important.

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:15.600
So please don't be cross because we must
work together to make the concert a success.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:22.270
Will I be able to memorise
all my 3 performances?

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.870
Oh, I have 3 performances too!

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:27.690
But the role of Queen that Jane
will play it's the most important one.

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:29.690
I can't believe that I was chosen.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:32.390
But I'll do my best to not disappoint everyone.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:35.690
But the Queen just needs
to stand there motionlessly,

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:38.030
it's a boring role that anyone can do.

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:40.600
You're right, Josie.

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:43.540
Thank goodness you're not taking this role.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:44.700
That's right.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.670
I've never heard of a fat Fairy Queen.

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:49.480
What are you saying?

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:53.100
I've never heard of a red-haired fairy either!

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:56.630
Isn't it nice to think that
fairies are all different?

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:59.570
Whether fat, skinny or red-haired.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:04.600
You're right. Now that we know our
roles, we'll have to do our best

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.980
because this is for the school flag.

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:09.590
Of course. I will do my best.

00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:11.870
Oh, I won't lose to you.

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.350
Me neither.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:17.090
My fairy friends, action!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:19.790
Let's do our best!

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:34.030
My tragic life!

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:34.750
Anne!

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:45.370
My tragic life!

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:50.750
Anne, w-what happened?

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:53.470
Marilla. How did it felt?

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:56.500
Did you felt that I had my heartbroken?

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:57.990
What are you saying?

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:01.950
I came in worried because
you sounded like you were dying!

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:03.810
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:05.470
But please don't be frightened.

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:08.200
I was just practicing for the concert drama.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:09.860
What concert?

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:11.940
Stop making strange animal-like noises.

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:15.580
But I won't sound like
that character unless I practice.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.370
I have to groan heartrendingly in one of them,

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.770
and it's really hard
to get up a good artistic groan.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.090
Groan heartrendingly?

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:23.200
Such nonsense.

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:26.580
I have no interest in rearing
animal-sounding actresses in this house!

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:28.930
Animal-sounding?

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:32.330
Then I still have a lot to practice.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:35.400
Please, stop!

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.060
I can't stand those screams!

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:41.410
Please practice anywhere, except in my house.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:45.970
I understand.
But I have others I need to practice for!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.010
I'm taking part in 4 performances.

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:53.140
A choir, two recitals, a dialogue and a tableau.

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:55.140
I'm to be Hope.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:20:01.880
And I am to be all draped in white with
my hands clasped--so--and my eyes uplifted.

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:06.650
Really.
I understand.

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:10.720
But don't forget the
housework and your studies.

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:14.020
Of course, Marilla.
I won't forget.

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:18.360
Although Anne had good intentions,

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:23.320
just as Marilla had worried,
Anne only thought about the concert.

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:26.800
She was always practicing and
couldn't concentrate in the houseworks.

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:34.620
Diana was also practicing her solo
because she didn't want to lose to Anne.

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:42.080
And the other children also improved
a great deal under Miss Stacy's guidance.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:50.860
But of course, Marilla disliked
Anne's passionate involvement.

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:58.270
So you came home late today too, Anne?

00:20:58.500 --> 00:20:59.340
I'm sorry.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:00.900
We had practice again today.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:05.350
You're wasting time with nonsense
that ought to be put on your lessons.

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:06.340
But...

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:12.650
I don't approve of children's getting
up concerts and racing about to practices.

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:17.720
It makes them vain
and forward and fond of gadding.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:21.170
But think of the worthy object.

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:24.290
A school flag will cultivate a
spirit of patriotism, Marilla.

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:25.370
Fudge!

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:29.340
There's precious little
patriotism in the thoughts of any of you.

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.420
All you want is a good time.

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:35.600
Well, when you can combine
patriotism and fun, isn't it all right?

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:41.330
Anne, all I want is you to behave yourself.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:45.660
I'll be heartily glad when all this fuss
is over and you'll be able to settle down.

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:49.500
You are simply good for nothing just now

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:55.140
with your head stuffed full of
dialogues and groans and tableaus.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:22:00.510
As for your tongue, it's
a marvel it's not clean worn out.

00:22:53.670 --> 00:22:55.390
What's wrong, Anne?

00:22:55.640 --> 00:23:01.860
Oh, Matthew... I think that rehearsing for
the concert is part of schoolwork, but...

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:05.730
Well now, I think the same.

00:23:05.730 --> 00:23:07.110
Really, Matthew?

00:23:07.510 --> 00:23:10.140
Do you understand how I feel?

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:16.870
Today we practiced the recital for
Mary, Queen of Scotland.

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:18.440
I'd like you to listen.

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:22.630
I put my whole soul into it.

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:25.260
On the way home Ruby Gillis
told me the way I said...

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:31.160
'Now for my father's soul
my woman's heart says farewell'

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:33.650
made her blood run cold!

00:23:33.650 --> 00:23:39.320
Well now, I would like you to recite it
for me one of these days in the barn.

00:23:39.320 --> 00:23:40.930
Oh, Matthew!

00:23:41.430 --> 00:23:44.590
But not at the barn.
Won't you come to the concert?

00:23:44.870 --> 00:23:50.920
Well now, I reckon it's going
to be a pretty good concert.

00:23:51.500 --> 00:23:56.690
And I expect you'll do your part fine.

00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:58.970
Thank you, Matthew!

00:24:00.050 --> 00:24:05.910
Now for my father's soul
my woman's heart says farewell.

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:13.410
The kind words from Matthew,
encouraged Anne again.

00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:23.680
As Matthew looks at Anne at her rehearsals,
he thought of a unrelated matter.

00:24:24.140 --> 00:24:26.730
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:29.180
Matthew and the Puffed Sleeves

00:24:29.180 --> 00:24:30.440
Please watch!
